# Call joins for documentation, as Kotlin's rewriteCallJoins: the
# `\callJoin:` symbol is dropped, nothing else changes. Input, then the tree
# from module::build_module in the form of print::write_ast.
# compat/check_ast.py --docs checks these against Kotlin.
=== if, else if and else, from Kotlin's stage test call-join-rewrite-for-docs
if (a) { b } else if (c) { d } else { e }
--- module
(Block
  (Call if a (Fun (Block b)) \else_if c (Fun (Block d)) \else (Fun (Block e))))

=== chained blocks with arguments
f(x) { a } g { b } h (y) { c }
--- module
(Block (Call f x (Fun (Block a)) \g (Fun (Block b)) \h y (Fun (Block c))))
